# Units never auto-enabled on systemd targets, even when their
# package is profiled.
#
# acpid: systemd-logind is the single ACPI event owner on SaphiraD
# targets (verified: logind handles the power button and virsh
# shutdown cleanly). acpid stays installed and available for roles
# that need custom event handling, but enabling both would double-
# handle every power event.
#
# saphira-network: systemd-networkd owns the base NIC on SaphiraD
# targets through the vendor default (generic wired DHCP match). The
# saphira framework service stays installed for roles and for
# firstboot-driven static setups, but must not run alongside
# networkd on the same interface.
acpid
saphira-network
